{"uid":"8dcc294755bfd1c5","name":"test_incurable_rejection_pause_is_in_memory_and_escalated_before_delivery","fullName":"tests.test_escalation_delivery#test_incurable_rejection_pause_is_in_memory_and_escalated_before_delivery","historyId":"48654157317e90f414ec79dd06646623","time":{"start":1791916146375,"stop":1791916146381,"duration":6},"description":"`rejected_incurable` is the ONE escalation site whose pause carries no\n    reason (`_pause_and_escalate_incurable_rejection` calls the bare\n    `self.pause()`, the same in-memory hold `POST /pause` takes), so SPEC\n    §4.6 promises it exactly this, and no more: the in-memory pause is\n    already in force and the `operator_escalation` event is already on\n    disk when the first delivery attempt runs, while status.json is not\n    rewritten to `paused` (`pauseReason` stays null). Its delivery is still\n    retried and still recorded undelivered, like every other site.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>rejected_incurable</code> is the ONE escalation site whose pause carries no<br />\nreason (<code>_pause_and_escalate_incurable_rejection</code> calls the bare<br />\n<code>self.pause()</code>, the same in-memory hold <code>POST /pause</code> takes), so SPEC<br />\n§4.6 promises it exactly this, and no more: the in-memory pause is<br />\nalready in force and the <code>operator_escalation</code> event is already on<br />\ndisk when the first delivery attempt runs, while status.json is not<br />\nrewritten to <code>paused</code> (<code>pauseReason</code> stays null). Its delivery is still<br />\nretried and still recorded undelivered, like every other site.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791916146346,"stop":1791916146347,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasCont